--- a/tenacity/releasenotes/notes/fix-wait-regressions-3b9e5d7a1c4f8206.yaml
+++ b/tenacity/releasenotes/notes/fix-wait-regressions-3b9e5d7a1c4f8206.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+---
+fixes:
+  - |
+    Falsy `wait` values such as `None`, `0` or `sum([])` mean "do not wait"
+    again for both `Retrying` and `AsyncRetrying`, instead of raising
+    `TypeError` from inside the retry loop on the first retry.
+  - |
+    Adding a plain callable to a wait strategy (`my_wait_func + wait_fixed(1)`)
+    builds a `wait_combine` again. A non-zero number on the left, such as
+    `5 + wait_fixed(1)`, is still rejected with `TypeError` at the addition,
+    and `sum()` over a list of wait strategies keeps working.
+  - |
+    `wait_combine` passes the retry state to each strategy positionally, as
+    the retry loop does, so a plain callable whose parameter is not named
+    `retry_state` can be combined with other waits.
